body:
Variable-length arrays using previous field values are not valid C syntax. Consider using a flexible array member or documenting this as pseudocode with proper C syntax showing how to access the variable-length data.
```suggestion
       // Pointer to SPDM certificate chain in slot 0.
       uint8_t *certificate0; // points to a buffer of certificate0_size bytes

       // ...

       // Size of certificate7, in bytes.
       uint32_t certificate7_size;

       // Pointer to SPDM certificate chain in slot 7.
       uint8_t *certificate7; // points to a buffer of certificate7_size bytes

       // Size of measurements, in bytes.
       uint32_t measurements_size;

       // Pointer to concatenation of GET_MEASUREMENTS and MEASUREMENTS as defined
       // in the SPDM specification.
       uint8_t *measurements; // points to a buffer of measurements_size bytes
```
